PRIVACY POLICY - IMG Measures

Last updated: November 3, 2026

This Privacy Policy describes how the IMG Measures app for Android
(package name: com.imgmeasures.app) handles your information.

In short: IMG Measures does not collect, transmit, sell or share any
personal data. Everything you create stays on your device.


1. DATA WE COLLECT

We do not collect any personal data. The app has no user accounts, no
analytics, no advertising, no crash reporting services and no
third-party tracking SDKs. The app does not request internet access and
does not send any data to us or to any third party.


2. PHOTOS AND CAMERA

- Picking photos: when you add a picture, the app uses the Android
  system photo picker. The app only receives the specific images you
  choose; it does not have access to the rest of your gallery.

- Taking photos: if you choose to take a photo, the app opens your
  device's camera app to capture it. IMG Measures does not request the
  camera permission itself.

- Imported images are copied into the app's private storage on your
  device so you can add measurements to them. The app reads the image's
  orientation information only to display it correctly.


3. DATA STORED ON YOUR DEVICE

The following information is stored locally, in the app's private
storage, and never leaves your device unless you decide to share or
export it:

- The images you import.
- The folders, measurements, annotations and notes you create.
- Your app preferences (for example theme and language).

You can delete this data at any time by deleting items inside the app,
by clearing the app's data in Android Settings, or by uninstalling the
app.


4. EXPORTING AND SHARING

When you choose to export or share your work:

- Exported files are saved to your device's public folders (for
  example Pictures/IMG_Measures or Downloads/IMG_Measures). On Android 9
  and lower, the storage permission is requested only for this purpose.
- Sharing uses the standard Android share menu. The files are sent only
  to the app or person you select. Any data you share this way is then
  handled by the receiving app or service under its own privacy policy.


5. DEVICE BACKUP

If Android backup is enabled on your device, your app data (images,
folders and measurements) may be included in your device's backup
(for example Google's backup service) or in a device-to-device
transfer. These backups are managed by Android and your backup
provider, not by us, and you can turn them off in your device settings.


6. PERMISSIONS

- Storage (Android 9 and lower only): to save exported files to public
  folders.
- Vibration: to provide haptic feedback while you use the editor.


7. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY

The app does not knowingly collect any personal information from
anyone, including children under the age of 13.


8. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will
be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date.


9. CONTACT

